Geometry Expert: To determine the length of the slackrope, we can model the situation as a triangle where the rope forms two segments. We know that the two poles are 15 m high and 14 m apart. Paul is standing 5 m from one of the poles and is 3 m above the ground. Let’s start by calculating the heights of the ropes on each side of Paul.

